{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-008", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Ireland approves 1,367 MW of solar in sixth renewables auction", "content": "<p>Ireland’s sixth onshore renewables auction (RESS 6) provisionally greenlit a total of 1,367 MW of solar across 22 projects, according to provisional results published by the grid operator. The weighted average offer price for PV was €0.10242 ($0.1121)/kWh.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/ress-6-provisional-results-solar-pv-ireland/\">Ireland approves 1,367 MW of solar in sixth renewables auction</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv maga", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/ress-6-provisional-results-solar-pv-ireland/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-009", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Italy awards 16 GWh of battery storage in second auction", "content": "<p>Italy's second Electricity Storage Capacity Procurement Mechanism (MACSE) auction awarded all 16 GWh of capacity offered for delivery in 2029, with a weighted average price 12% below the level recorded in the previous auction.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/italy-awards-16-gwh-of-battery-storage-in-second-auction/\">Italy awards 16 GWh of battery storage in second auction</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/italy-awards-16-gwh-of-battery-storage-in-second-auction/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-010", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "UtmoLight, UNSW achieve 19.6% efficiency for 2.81 m² perovskite solar module", "content": "<p>The reported result corresponds to a power output of around 551 W and represents a 15% relative efficiency increase over UtmoLight’s previous benchmark. The module was tested at Germany’s Fraunhofer Institute for Solar Energy Systems (Fraunhofer ISE).</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/utmolight-unsw-achieve-19-6-efficiency-for-2-81-m%c2%b2-perovskite-solar-module/\">UtmoLight, UNSW achieve 19.6% efficiency for 2.81 m² perovskite solar module</a> appeared first on ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/utmolight-unsw-achieve-19-6-efficiency-for-2-81-m%c2%b2-perovskite-solar-module/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-011", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Poweroad unveils modular LFP battery system with up to 245.76 kWh of storage", "content": "<p>Poweroad's new battery storage system is available in high- and low-voltage configurations and features 5.12 kWh lithium iron phosphate (LFP) battery modules based on CATL cells. The high-voltage version can also be equipped with a 20 kW electric vehicle charger.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/poweroad-unveils-modular-lfp-battery-system-with-up-to-245-76-kwh-of-storage/\">Poweroad unveils modular LFP battery system with up to 245.76 kWh of storage</a> appeared ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/poweroad-unveils-modular-lfp-battery-system-with-up-to-245-76-kwh-of-storage/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-012", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "UK small-scale battery deployment set to double annual record in 2026", "content": "<p>Deployment data from certification body MCS reveals small-scale battery storage installations in 2026 are close to doubling annual record set in 2026. Policy support expected to fuel further growth in 2027.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/uk-small-scale-battery-deployment-set-to-double-annual-record-in-2026/\">UK small-scale battery deployment set to double annual record in 2026</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.<", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/uk-small-scale-battery-deployment-set-to-double-annual-record-in-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-013", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Afore unveils all-in-one propane heat pump for residential applications", "content": "<p>The new air-to-water heat pump series features nominal heating capacities ranging from 8.03 kW to 11.75 kW and coefficients of performance of up to 5.70. The systems can achieve an outlet water temperature of up to 75 C.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/afore-unveils-all-in-one-propane-heat-pump-for-residential-applications/\">Afore unveils all-in-one propane heat pump for residential applications</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv mag", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/afore-unveils-all-in-one-propane-heat-pump-for-residential-applications/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-25-014", "date": "2026-11-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["leading", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Belgium forecast to reach 28.6 GW of solar by 2035", "content": "<p>GlobalData expects Belgium’s solar capacity to more than double from 2025 levels, with distributed installations leading growth amid rising electricity demand and declining nuclear capacity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/belgium-forecast-to-reach-28-6-gw-of-solar-by-2035/\">Belgium forecast to reach 28.6 GW of solar by 2035</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/25/belgium-forecast-to-reach-28-6-gw-of-solar-by-2035/", "type": "rss"}]}
